    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`/tokenize` and chat don't encode the same request when `reasoning_effort` is in `chat_template_kwargs`. Chat moves it onto the request before rendering; tokenize skips that step. On DeepSeek-V4.1, `thinking=true` with `reasoning_effort=low` renders budget 50 through chat and 75 through tokenize.\n\n## Modifications\n\nMove the existing effort handling into `_prepare_reasoning_effort` and call it from both paths. Hunyuan still uses its own handling.\n\n## Testing\n\n- The new regression compares the full input token IDs for `low`, `max`, a numeric budget, and kwargs overriding the top-level effort. All four cases fail on main and pass with this change.\n- DeepSeek serving and renderer, protocol, and chat unit tests: 220 passed, plus 220 subtests.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40324648753](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40324648753)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40324648775](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40324648775)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40324648962](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40324648962)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
